## 6. A/B experiment

### Design document

- **Hypothesis.** Sending a {{ ab.effect_model.discount | pct(0) }} coupon to the users in the top
  {{ ab.effect_model.top_deciles }} propensity decile(s) increases next-7-day conversion.
- **Unit and assignment.** User; deterministic SHA-256 hash of `salt:user_id`, 50/50 split
  (`src/ecom/experiment/simulate_ab.py`). The salt was chosen **before launch** by a seedfinder
  search over candidate salts, using only assignment counts and pre-period covariates
  (balance criteria: SRM p >= {{ d.salt_search.criteria.min_srm_p }}, |standardized mean
  difference| <= {{ d.salt_search.criteria.max_abs_smd }} on pre-spend, propensity and sessions):
  `{{ d.salt }}` after {{ d.salt_search.candidates_tried }} candidate(s).
- **Population.** Users active in the 21 days before {{ cfg.labels.splits.test }} (held-out test
  snapshot; no model has seen their outcomes): {{ d.population | num }} users.
- **Primary metric.** Conversion (share of users who purchase within 7 days), analysed
  intention-to-treat over the whole arm.
- **Guardrails.** Revenue per user (must not drop significantly) and buyer average order value
  (must not drop by more than {{ cfg.experiment.max_aov_drop | pct(0) }}).
- **Error rates.** alpha = {{ d.alpha }}, power = {{ d.power | pct(0) }}, minimum detectable
  effect = {{ d.mde_relative | pct(0) }} relative on a baseline of {{ d.baseline_rate | pct(2) }}.
- **Sample size** (`statsmodels` `NormalIndPower`, Cohen's h = {{ d.effect_size_h | num(4) }}):
  **{{ d.n_per_arm | num }} users per arm**{% if d.duration_days %}, i.e. about
  **{{ d.duration_days }} days** at {{ d.daily_eligible_users | num }} eligible users per day{% endif %}.
  This run has {{ d.n_per_arm_available | num }} per arm, so its MDE is
  {{ d.mde_at_available_n | pct(1) }} (power {{ d.power_at_available_n | pct(0) }} for a
  {{ d.mde_relative | pct(0) }} lift){% if d.power_at_available_n < 0.8 %} - underpowered for the
  design MDE, which the decision has to respect{% endif %}.

**Simulation assumptions** (the effect is simulated; outcomes in control are observed data):
the coupon multiplies a targeted user's purchase odds by `1 + {{ ab.effect_model.base_uplift }} x s`,
where `s` is the user's price-sensitivity percentile and the baseline probability is the
calibrated model score; newly converted users spend their average viewed price minus the
discount; users who would have bought anyway still redeem it (the cost the guardrails watch).

