**Peeking pitfall.** In {{ ab.peeking.n_simulations }} A/A tests on the untreated outcomes,
checking the p-value after each of the {{ ab.peeking.looks }} days and stopping at the first
p < 0.05 produced a false-positive rate of **{{ ab.peeking.fpr_any_look | pct(1) }}** instead of
{{ ab.peeking.fpr_final_look_only | pct(1) }} for a single look at the planned end. Keeping the
family-wise rate at 5% with daily looks needs a per-look threshold of about
{{ ab.peeking.empirical_pocock_threshold | num(4) }} (an empirical Pocock boundary) - or simply a
fixed horizon.

